    "expectedRule": "Chapter 4 pollution (0-4). Any first node clear that dealt damage raises pollution by 1 and a harmless clear leaves it; clearing pharmacy_reward lowers it by 1; an event outcome that deals damage raises it by 1 and succeeding at triage_ward lowers it by 1; the result is clamped to 0-4. Display: title 锈疫污染, status `污染 n/4`, severity stable at 0, warning at 1-2, danger at 3-4, meter {n, 4}, targetReached at 0. At pollution 3 healing is -10% and enemy art power +10%; at 4 they are -20% and +20%. triage_ward: burn_focus_incense without incense fails for 26 damage; sterilize_with_iron_body succeeds without damage when iron_body is equipped (here the support method, picked as the next learned method). With mist_breathing as the main method every trap is seen through and iron_body cuts the rest by 20%, so a risked trap deals max(4, floor(damage x 0.45 x 0.8)): rust_gurney_trap 34 -> 12, disinfectant_mist_trap 36 -> 12, sterile_corridor 38 -> 13. Run pressure stays 0% below 6 clears. Gates open at pollution at most: hospital_pristine_isolation_corridor 0, hospital_clean_sterile_corridor 1, hospital_clean_roof_lane 2, hospital_emergency_antidote_corridor 3; a closed one reads `污染需降至 n 或以下；先去药房抽屉或完成分诊净化。`. plague_orderly (80 HP) outlives the first strike, and a surviving monster always lands at least 1 damage. The pursuer is a separate run system and is disabled after entry so it cannot ambush the walk. All expected values are frozen here, never read from candidate code."
  },
